I have been informed by the Chairman of the Prices and Incomes Commission as follows: 1. The names of the research economists who have accepted positions with the Prices and Incomes Commission and the dates they indicated their acceptance are as follows:
Mr. D. Brazier,	May 23, 1969;
Mr. H. Bubeck,	July 30, 1969;
Questions
Mr. J. Cragg, June 15, 1969;
Mr. W. Dymond, July 11, 1969;
Mr. J. Hague, June 25, 1969;
Mr. T. Houston, August 6, 1969;
Mr. L. Reed, June 22, 1969.
2. The Commission does not maintain a record of preliminary approaches to economists in academic institutions.
